; `tan` is host-independent: routed through `src/trig.zig` (musl/
; compiler_rt software impl), not the platform-libm `@tan` builtin, so the
; native build and both WASM artifacts agree bit-for-bit. Pinned decimals
; are the canonical `{d}` rendering. Form 1 (x = 100) exercises the
; Payne-Hanek large-argument reduction.
(tan 1.0)
(tan 100.0)
